{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods","id":904558,"title":"Minor/Embarrassing Gods","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-31T16:44:23-07:00","id":904558,"title":"Minor/Embarrassing Gods","content":"Looking at the april fools book and in some of the supplements, I have to say that one of the roleplaying premises i find the most intriguing is to play a scion of an embarassing or really minor god. Like the always mentioned latrine related gods, or someone like Caligula. Therefor I hope such minor deities make a comback in the second edition of scion <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Does anyone else have an input on the subject? Like for example how should such minor deities be stated compared to their more esteemed and important counterparts, or how many favored boons/skills should the children of such gods receive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T17:27:57-07:00","id":904580,"title":"","content":"Well there's always Priapus for the Theoi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:45:24-07:00","id":904624,"title":"","content":"I find the children of Nyx and her daughter Eris to be pretty good choices for minor/embarrassing gods<br /> <br /> Nyx<br /> -Ker: female gods of violent or cruel death, including death in battle, by accident, murder or ravaging disease<br /> -Hypnos: god of sleep<br /> -The Oneiro: gods of dreams Phobetor/Morphues<br /> -Momous: god of mockery<br /> -Oizys: god of misery<br /> -Apate: goddess of deceit<br /> -Philot\u00eas: god of friendship and affection<br /> -Geras: god of old age<br /> -Sophrosyne: goddess of moderation<br /> -Epiphron: god of prudence<br /> -Hybrys: goddess of insolence, violence and wantonness<br /> <br /> Eris<br /> -Ponos: god of labour and toil<br /> -Lethe: goddess of forgetfulness<br /> -Limos: god of hunger, famine and starvation<br /> -Dysnomia: goddess of lawlessness<br /> -Ate: goddess of delusion, blind folly, rash action<br /> <br /> I'm really not a fan of saying that your god parent is better/lesser than mine so I get more/fewer points. All characters start out at the same legend with the same potential to do awesome things. Having a parent that is the god of old age or moderation would limit you in the beginning compared to being the child of Odin but from what I understand you can change that later on so it is all good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T18:52:38-07:00","id":904629,"title":"","content":"I don't know, being a God of Mockery sounds like a pretty sweet deal.<br /> <br /> You can deride and humiliate anybody in the multiverse and say &quot;just doing my job!&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T19:08:44-07:00","id":904640,"title":"","content":"Yeah he tried that with the Theoi. Zeus kicked him off the mountain and said go do your job elsewhere.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:47:45-07:00","id":904691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Achilles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=904640#post904640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah he tried that with the Theoi. Zeus kicked him off the mountain and said go do your job elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The Theoi are the Greeks, right? I use the pantheon names from the books, so it confuses me when I see people throwing out these alternative names for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T20:59:15-07:00","id":904695,"title":"","content":"Yes, the Theoi are Greeks. Dodekathon is just the 12 Olympians that were in leadership positions. Theoi=gods, so more inclusive of everyone living on Mount Olympus and beyond.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-31T22:37:06-07:00","id":904730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=904691#post904691\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The Theoi are the Greeks, right? I use the pantheon names from the books, so it confuses me when I see people throwing out these alternative names for them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoi is also the name of the shared Etruscan-Greek-Roman Pantheon we'll be seeing in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-01T06:13:44-07:00","id":904905,"title":"","content":"I don't remember the name of the norse goddess from the april fools book, but she is one of Friggs handmaidens. Think about that for drama being born with the same potential as a daughter or son of Odin, but at the same time with so much less opportunity to fully exploit that potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:33:28-07:00","id":905474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=904905#post904905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember the name of the norse goddess from the april fools book, but she is one of Friggs handmaidens. Think about that for drama being born with the same potential as a daughter or son of Odin, but at the same time with so much less opportunity to fully exploit that potential.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You can get the same narrative from the Theoi with Hebe. She's literally a daughter of Zeus and Hera! And she ends up the cupbearer of the gods, until she gets fired to make room for her dad's boytoy (Ganymede)!<br /> <br /> She's pouring the drinks on the summit of Mount Olympus for her half-siblings who are the children of lesser Titans (Athena, Apollo, Artemis), a nymph (Hermes), parthenogenesis (Hephaestus), and a mortal (Dionysus)!* She's one of the only children of the reigning KING AND QUEEN OF THE UNIVERSE, and she's the cupbearing minor goddess of youth.<br /> <br /> *Aphrodite may or may not belong on this list too - I tend to favor the Zeus/Dione version over the Ouranos/seafoam version, just because of the LACK of &quot;Zeus tries to bang Aphrodite&quot; myths, which implies to me she was widely seen as his daughter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T01:40:55-07:00","id":905477,"title":"","content":"Yeah that is also a great one. I just prefer minor gods and goddesses to be honest. &lt;.&lt; I am also the sort of scion player that would advocate for the player band to make their own pantheon when reaching godhood","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T06:49:26-07:00","id":905590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=905474#post905474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> *Aphrodite may or may not belong on this list too - I tend to favor the Zeus/Dione version over the Ouranos/seafoam version, just because of the LACK of &quot;Zeus tries to bang Aphrodite&quot; myths, which implies to me she was widely seen as his daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What's hilarious about that is she's the patron goddess of prostitutes, and Zeus didn't try to touch her. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T09:06:05-07:00","id":905688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=905474#post905474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> You can get the same narrative from the Theoi with Hebe. She's literally a daughter of Zeus and Hera! And she ends up the cupbearer of the gods, until she gets fired to make room for her dad's boytoy (Ganymede)!<br /> <br /> She's pouring the drinks on the summit of Mount Olympus for her half-siblings who are the children of lesser Titans (Athena, Apollo, Artemis), a nymph (Hermes), parthenogenesis (Hephaestus), and a mortal (Dionysus)!* She's one of the only children of the reigning KING AND QUEEN OF THE UNIVERSE, and she's the cupbearing minor goddess of youth.<br /> <br /> *Aphrodite may or may not belong on this list too - I tend to favor the Zeus/Dione version over the Ouranos/seafoam version, just because of the LACK of &quot;Zeus tries to bang Aphrodite&quot; myths, which implies to me she was widely seen as his daughter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.. if you actually ARE holding to a more Athenian version of Hephaestus (and also a Homeric one), Hephaestus isn't parthogenetic (&quot;hatched&quot; from Hera as a rebuke for the sua sponte birth of Athena). He's also the son of Hera an Zeus, full brother to Ares and Hebe. Which is how he was present to wield the axe to split daddy's head for the also not-so-parthogenetic Athena, daughter of Metis-the-swallowed-fly-first-wife.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:08:54-07:00","id":905737,"title":"","content":"As the developer of Scion Extras I approve of this thread. I ran a one-shot using the characters we created for Scion Extras. It was a bit silly, but tons of fun.<br /> <br /> -Matt","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Owner/Editor - FlamesRising.com","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/949-matt-m-mcelroy","name":"Matt-M-McElroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar949_2.jpeg","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"246"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T10:34:14-07:00","id":905756,"title":"","content":"SO YOU ARE THE ONE TO BLAME FOR SCION STYLE? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Anyway i liked the book ignoring scion style <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T14:44:09-07:00","id":905965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=905477#post905477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah that is also a great one. I just prefer minor gods and goddesses to be honest. &lt;.&lt; I am also the sort of scion player that would advocate for the player band to make their own pantheon when reaching godhood</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never gotten to that point in any of my Sciong games but I had many ideas for new pantheons. If you've read A Madness of Angels, we had a group who were working towards making themselves a pantheon based on the spirits from that. Like a more modern version of the Loa, with Lady Neon who rules the nightlife, the Blue Electric Angel(s) who are the embodiment of the life in the wires and technology and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-20T07:47:56-07:00","id":918034,"title":"","content":"how about some Norse examples.<br /> What about Mimir? A beheaded god known for being wise/being used as a captive/ and losing body parts. Best of all, he's just a head, pretty sure the scion was adopted...<br /> <br /> Now he is dead, but it could make an interesting tale if you could make it work (maybe Hel gave him a day free?) but Kvasir is made of all the spit of the gods and name means spit, he was wise and powerful and blood is the mead of inspiration after he died.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11938-3comrades","name":"3Comrades","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T00:15:13-07:00","id":920231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=904629#post904629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know, being a God of Mockery sounds like a pretty sweet deal.<br /> <br /> You can deride and humiliate anybody in the multiverse and say &quot;just doing my job!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Cairbre, of the Tuatha, was a bard/satirist whose mockery of Bres caused him to magically lose his luck, his wealth, and his kingship. Cairbre's polemic against Bres basically lead to Nuada becoming High King. So yeah, God of Mockery can be pretty badass (and reeeeally fun to roleplay).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://twitter.com/carykingdom\" target=\"_blank\">@CaryKingdom </a>- Writer and Ne'er-do-well<br /> Deititian at <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/scion/\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Second Edition</a><br /> Storyguide of <a href=\"https://scabbyrooster.fandom.com/wiki/The_Demi_Dozen\" target=\"_blank\">The Demi Dozen</a>, a Hero-level, live-streamed Scion Campaign<br /> Everything is subject to change; all opinions expressed are solely my own or those of my houseplants.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1093-arlecchino","name":"Arlecchino","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T09:18:42-07:00","id":920404,"title":"","content":"Andhrimnir, <i>Cook </i>of the Aesir.<br /> Elli - goddess of old age<br /> Fulla - handmaiden of Frigg, not even a goddess of anything.<br /> Hlin - goddess of consolation &quot;there, there little Viking, it's okay, you'll pillage more next time&quot;<br /> Hoenir - the silent god........yeah, that's it.<br /> Nerpus - goddess of.....um, we don't really know because some poet just dropped her name and walked away.<br /> Skaoi - goddess of winter.......bitch, it's ALWAYS cold here!<br /> Vali - god of revenge, minor but could be a real SOB<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-25T07:24:13-07:00","id":920945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Papa Bear</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/904558-minor-embarrassing-gods?p=920404#post920404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Andhrimnir, <i>Cook </i>of the Aesir.<br /> Elli - goddess of old age<br /> Fulla - handmaiden of Frigg, not even a goddess of anything.<br /> Hlin - goddess of consolation &quot;there, there little Viking, it's okay, you'll pillage more next time&quot;<br /> Hoenir - the silent god........yeah, that's it.<br /> Nerpus - goddess of.....um, we don't really know because some poet just dropped her name and walked away.<br /> Skaoi - goddess of winter.......bitch, it's ALWAYS cold here!<br /> Vali - god of revenge, minor but could be a real SOB</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> How is the Aesir's cook a humiliating position? Their whole deal was fighting and feasting!<br /> <br /> As for Skaoi, probably don't want to piss off the one who could potentially cause the Long Winter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}